 e.\nThe predicted edge passes 4 km to the N\, so a miss is likely — but 
 a chord from near the edge is the most valuable observation of all.\nClose
 st approach 04:20:35 IST\, give or take 2 s. The star is 35° up in the WS
 W · dusk.\nIt fades 2.5 magnitudes for up to 5.5 s on the centre line\, a
 nd the path is 62 km wide\, give or take 32 km.\nThe map\, the finder char
 t and the path as KML: https://occult.alokm.com/asteroid?e=2027-07-03-792-
 metcalfia-146048
